-changes and why. `git log v6.6..HEAD` is the whole THOX story — that
-one command is the audit surface. In v0.1.0 the configuration is
-published as per-class config *fragments* (intent, under `configs/`
-in the linux-thox package); the defconfig files are generated from
-those fragments at the first import.
+linux-thox is intended to be the kernel ThoxOS Core runs. It is a Linux
+LTS fork, licensed GPL-2.0-only, and it is deliberately not a new kernel:
+the THOX delta on top of upstream Linux is meant to be a readable patch
+series plus published configuration files. In v0.1.0 that series is empty
+and this repository has no `v6.6` tag, so `git log v6.6..HEAD` is not an
+audit surface yet. The configuration is published as per-class config
+fragments (intent, under `configs/`); the defconfig files are generated
+from those fragments at the first import.
 
 | Base | Used for | Why |
 | --- | --- | --- |
 | Linux 6.6 LTS (v0.1.0 pin: 6.6.161) | Device classes E2, P4, P6 | Long-term support series, programme-locked for devices until a device-qualification cycle justifies moving |
 | Linux 6.12 LTS (v0.1.0 pin: 6.12.115) | Desktop class | Current long-term support series for the Desktop Edition (Debian 13 userland, COSMIC desktop) |
 
-Full source accompanies every binary image, with the GPL source
-offer, at release.
+v0.1.0 publishes this packaging tree, not a binary kernel image. When a
+binary image is released, GPL-2.0-only requires the corresponding complete
+source to accompany it.
 
